-- title:
--   Inertia at q with v_q(M)=2 is non-tame of order ∤ q-1
-- statement:
--   Let $M\neq 0$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form for $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform: $g$ is a normalised Hecke eigenform ($q$-coefficient $1$ at $1$, multiplicative at coprime indices, with the usual recursions at prime powers) and no proper divisor of $M$ carries a normalised eigenform whose $q$-coefficients agree with those of $g$ at all primes not dividing $M$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime with $\lambda\neq 2$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, and let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal topology, with finite residue field, in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(M))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, and the $U_p$ for primes $p\mid M$, $p\notin S$) to $\mathbb C$ sending each such $T_\ell$ to the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient of $g$, let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $O'$, and let $\rho$ be an adically continuous representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (the $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) on a free $O'$-module of rank $2$ whose residual representation, obtained by tensoring with the residue field, is irreducible and odd (every non-trivial involution has determinant $-1$) and which satisfies: for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X+\ell$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq\lambda$, $q\equiv-1\pmod\lambda$ and $M$-adic valuation $v_q(M)=2$. Let $\Phi$ be a non-zero complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb Q$ which is an adelic lift of $g$ in the sense of [`CuspForm.IsAdelicLiftOf`](def/CuspForm_AdelicLift.html#L14) (invariant on the left under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q)$, invariant on the right under the finite level-one subgroup for the ideal $(M)$, and given at elements with trivial finite part and positive-determinant archimedean part by the weight-two slash of $g$ evaluated at $i$), and assume that for all characters $\mu_1,\mu_2:\mathbb Q_q^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ every $\mathbb C$-linear, $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$-equivariant map from the span of the adelic translates of $\Phi$ to the principal series [`LocalNewvector.PSCarrier q μ₁ μ₂`](def/LocalNewvector_PrincipalSeriesCarrier.html#L173) vanishes. Then there exist a local domain $O''$, an injective local ring homomorphism $j:O'\to O''$ and a function $a$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $O''^\times$ such that, for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $q$ as a non-unit, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ maps under $j$ to $(X-a(\sigma))(X-a(\sigma)^{-1})$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, and some $\sigma$ in that inertia subgroup satisfies $a(\sigma)^{q-1}\neq 1$.
--
--   This is the local-global compatibility input at a prime dividing the level exactly twice, in the form needed for the supercuspidal branch of level lowering: inertia at $q$ acts on the $\lambda$-adic representation of the newform with eigenvalues $a(\sigma),a(\sigma)^{-1}$ after a faithful local extension of coefficients, and the character $a$ is not killed by $q-1$, so the local behaviour is not that of an unramified twist of a principal series or of Steinberg type. It feeds the construction of Hecke eigensystems comparing a semistable elliptic curve with a modular form, via [`WeierstrassCurve.isEigensystemH1_comp_apOfModel_of_isSemistableModel_of_qCoeff_congr_of_steinberg_quotient`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.isEigensystemH1_comp_apOfModel_of_isSemistableModel_of_qCoeff_congr_of_steinberg_quotient).
